# IT Risk Register
## NIST 800-30 and HIPAA Security Rule Focus

## Overview

This portfolio case study uses a fictionalized healthcare scenario, **Cedar Park Regional Health (CPRH)**, to demonstrate practical Governance, Risk, and Compliance skills in a regional pediatric and acute care environment.

The purpose of this project is to show how technical security concepts can be translated into business-ready risk documentation, audit preparation, control remediation, and vendor risk oversight. The artifacts below reflect common responsibilities for an entry-level GRC analyst supporting healthcare security and compliance programs.

---

## Project Objectives

- Demonstrate foundational GRC and cybersecurity risk management concepts
- Practice documenting organizational and technical risks
- Apply HIPAA Security Rule and NIST 800-30 principles
- Develop business-focused remediation recommendations
- Simulate real-world healthcare compliance workflows

